/*==============================================================================
 = QWN FILE HEADER -- qwn_exdes.v (module name kept "clock_test_exdes" so the
 = Vivado project top setting and the wizard hierarchy still apply)
 =
 = ROLE IN THE SYSTEM
 =   Top level of the QWN bufferless oversampling link on the VC709
 =   (xc7vx690tffg1761-2, Vivado 2023.2). Two boards (C16A TX-side rig, C6A
 =   RX) run this same bitstream, linked gt0<->gt0 over duplex fiber (SFP
 =   cage 0). The GT serial line runs at 10 Gb/s but carries 1.25 Gb/s
 =   8B/10B data: the GT RX is a RAW 64-bit oversampler (RXBUF_EN=FALSE,
 =   RXOUTCLKSEL=RXOUTCLKPMA) and ALL clock/data recovery, comma alignment,
 =   8B/10B decode, header parse and gate timing happen in fabric (inside
 =   qwn_rx_lane). TX streams a pre-encoded periodic burst (~26 us period):
 =   K28.5 warmup, settle, FID byte 0x6B, 8-byte header, payload, trailer,
 =   then a laser-off dark gap. The deliverable signal is the payload-start
 =   MARKER on pin N41 (FMC LA02_N), placed to sub-UI precision; the design
 =   invariant is "missing gate, never a wrong gate".
 =
 =   This file is the generated wizard example-design shell (support wrapper
 =   instance, reset synchronizers, DRP clock buffers) with the original
 =   frame_gen/frame_check/ChipScope blocks stripped (work/integrate_exdes.py)
 =   and the QWN fabric grafted in below the generated boilerplate. The long
 =   runs of blank lines mark where generated code was removed -- left as-is
 =   so diffs against a freshly generated exdes stay readable.
 =
 = LANE MAP (all four GTs of quad 113, clock region X1Y3)
 =   gt0 = lane 0 "signal": full TX + RX recovery; marker -> N41.
 =   gt1 = lane 1 "idler" : full TX + RX recovery; marker -> H41 (dark on the
 =         current bench; doubles as the legacy-path A/B reference).
 =   gt2 = TX-ONLY inter-board source (C16A cage-2 -> fiber -> C6A SFP0);
 =         clocked from gt0's TX clocks (a third full RX lane cannot place:
 =         7-series caps 12 clock tracks per region and per-lane bufferless
 =         RX clocking is irreducible -- see MIGRATION_PLAN "LEVER B").
 =         Its TX fiducial drives TX_PAYLOAD_REF on H31 (LA27_N) = the
 =         scope reference for the single-shot jitter figure (N41 - H31).
 =   gt3 = spare (data tied to 0).
 =
 = CLOCK DOMAINS (FPGA basics: every GT lane has its own recovered clock;
 =   nothing here is "the" system clock)
 =   drpclk_in_i      156.25 MHz free-running (board feed via DRP_CLK_IN_*);
 =                    JTAG/VIO/counters domain -- alive even when links die.
 =   gtN_txusrclk2_i  156.25 MHz from each TX MMCM off TXOUTCLK.
 =   gtN_rxusrclk2_i  156.25 MHz RECOVERED clock from the RX MMCM off
 =                    RXOUTCLK(PMA). Everything per-burst lives here.
 =   gt0_rxusrclk625_i 625 MHz, SAME gt0 RX MMCM (CLK2_OUT, divide-1 = VCO).
 =                    OSERDES bit clock for the marker (B10 de-cascade).
 =   idelay_ref200    200 MHz synthesized from drpclk by a dedicated MMCM
 =                    (IDELAYCTRL reference; drpclk itself is NOT 200 MHz).
 =
 = BUILD CHRONOLOGY relevant to THIS file (2026-06 marker-jitter campaign;
 =   bitstreams/ has every build + README; sigma = scope single-shot N41-H31)
 =   Build A  (p_a)  ui_offset detection exported into probe_in17 packing.
 =   Build B/B2      mark_oserdes integer-UI slot relaunch + ODELAY trim
 =                   (B was dead-on-pin: OSERDES TQ/tristate pitfall -- see
 =                   the marker block below).            sigma 8-stripe ~2 ns
 =   B3              coarse/fine borrow (in qwn_rx_lane). sigma 528 ps
 =   B4              gate_ui commit latch + CLOCK_DELAY_GROUP. (480 ps)
 =   B5              gate_pending hold-reopen deferral (in lane).
 =   B6              occurrence counters on hist idx12/idx13 (this file).
 =   B7              HOLD_FOREVER RXCDRHOLD policy (in lane). sigma 122 ps
 =   B8              filtered eph split-role trim + FAST slew. sigma 88.4 ps
 =                   (device ~82 ps after removing 27.7 ps scope noise)
 =   B9              veto v1 -- negative result kept in record (14.75%
 =                   vetoed, zero benefit); veto counter on idx11 (here).
 =   B10/B11         MMCM DE-CASCADE: marker MMCM + 3 BUFGs deleted; the
 =                   OSERDES pair now comes from the gt0 RX MMCM itself
 =                   (EDITED GENERATED FILES clock_test_support.v /
 =                   clock_test_gt_usrclk_source.v -- DO NOT regenerate the
 =                   clock_test IP). B11 retunes VETO_TH 24->48 (in lane).
 =                   B11 JTAG-validated; analog verdict pending bench.
 =
 = EVIDENCE
 =   Sim: tb_mark_oserdes, tb_uioff_e2e, tb_stale_ui, tb_holdgate(2),
 =        tb_eph_jitter, tb_subui_sweep, tb_e2e_hw (the keystone oracle).
 =   HW : work/scope CSV evidence chain (b4_run1 ... b9_final, b11 pend.),
 =        qwn_jitter_campaign_2026-06-10.png; VIO dose-response experiment
 =        (see vio_cdrhold_mode below) that identified CDR re-acquisition
 =        grid displacement as the straggler mechanism.
 =
 = COMPANION FILES
 =   qwn_rx_lane.v (per-lane RX recovery: CDR/frame/header/gate/hold policy),
 =   mark_oserdes.v, mark_odelay.v, eph_filter.v, phase_hist.v, qwn_dbg.v,
